And the venture capitalists who gave them the money wanted them to do two things, which are about going fast. One was to hire people. And the other thing was to do more product development. But the thing that Noam and his team figured out was that when people downloaded the software, a month later none of them were using it. So there was a problem. So what he did was he stopped the whole company, used sort of an automotive analogy, hit the brakes, and did both quantitative and qualitative analysis about why people aren't keeping our

