software and did no hiring and no product development. He made a list. He called it the MIT list, the most important thing list. Once they had that list, if you will, they hit the gas. They started hiring people and doing product development. Once they figured out what needed to be done, and this is very much out of Daniel Kahneman stuff on fast and slow, that when you're in a cognitive mind field, you don't rush ahead. Sometimes it's better just to stand there

